<VI _name="t209_stacked_sequence_locals.vi" description="&lt;p&gt;Works on the assumption that &lt;strong&gt;ordered x array&lt;/strong&gt; is in monotonically increasing or decreasing order and can therefore efficiently search for the relative index of the location of &lt;strong&gt;x value&lt;/strong&gt; within the &lt;strong&gt;x array&lt;/strong&gt;. The VI starts the search at the &lt;strong&gt;starting index&lt;/strong&gt; and begins by using a fast hunting phase to roughly bracket the location and then narrows to the final bracket using a bisection search. The VI computes the &lt;strong&gt;fractional index&lt;/strong&gt; location by using linear interpolation.&lt;/p&gt;">
  <Control _name="ordered x array" type="array{double.Numeric}" description="&lt;strong&gt;ordered x array&lt;/strong&gt; is the array of tabulated values of the dependent variable and must be monotonically increasing or decreasing." uid="1942" uid_parent="root" value="[]" conIdx="11" connection="recommended" outputs="value:1942.value" />
  <Control _name="starting index" type="int32" description="&lt;strong&gt;starting index&lt;/strong&gt; is the assumed initial search location. This value is usually set to the index of a previous search when the values to locate tend to be near each other in subsequent searches. The closer the starting index is to the true location of &lt;strong&gt;x value&lt;/strong&gt;\2C the faster the search." uid="46" uid_parent="root" value="0" conIdx="9" connection="recommended" outputs="value:46.value" />
